- The same Reuters Institute report also notes coordinated DDoS attacks on major Philippine news sites.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines | Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/digital-news-report/2022/philippines","claim":"The report says coordinated DDoS attacks crippled major Philippine news organizations, including Rappler, Vera Files, ABS-CBN, GMA News, CNN Philippines, and others.","locator":"lines 39-40","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Same study, different materially distinct claim with specific list of affected outlets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 campaign-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Contextual rather than directly ordered by Marcos, but it reflects the hostile information environment around his rise.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not attribute every attack to Marcos personally.","It describes environment and incidents, not a completed policy of state censorship."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

- [‘A disservice to voters’: Marcos snubs KBP, other presidential interviews to control narrative](https://pcij.org/2022/02/04/marcos-snubs-kbp-other-presidential-interviews-to-control-narrative/) is direct evidence of selective media engagement.
